//go:build protocoldef

package protocoldef

// EntitySyncPush carries one server-authoritative state frame for the scene:
// the players this client is subscribed to, as encoded by roost-core's room
// transport sink. The demo pushes it over the player's TCP connection; a UDP
// or KCP deployment sends the same bytes, and the deltas as real datagrams.
//
// Two lanes are folded into one message on purpose. Snapshots and removals
// are reliable frames and arrive whole (Datagram=false). Deltas are fragments
// of one frame (Datagram=true): a client feeds them to
// statesync.NewReassembler in arrival order and decodes the frame once it is
// complete. Both end at room.DecodeRoomWireFrame, then
// room.DecodeRoomSubjectUpdate per object — the subject id says whose state
// it is, and the payload is what that entity's packer produced.
type EntitySyncPush struct {
	Datagram bool   `pb:"1"`
	Payload  []byte `pb:"2"`
}

//roost:protocol group=game handler=player
type EntitySyncProtocol interface {
	//roost:msg id=10103
	EntitySync() EntitySyncPush
}
